# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Blueprint 5 — The Connected Boardroom (Collaborative Specialist Networks)
# environment template
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Copy this file:      cp .env.example .env
# 2. Paste your real key into .env (NOT into this file).
# 3. Never commit .env.  Add it to .gitignore before your first commit.
#
# If you already did this for Chapters 1-4, you are done — this chapter
# reuses the exact same key and the exact same .env. No new setup, no new
# environment variable, nothing to add. Every specialist call and every
# Supervisor turn in this chapter still authenticates with one
# GEMINI_API_KEY against one model, MODEL, defined once in
# examples/_common.py.
#
# A leaked Gemini API key is a billable key. If you ever paste one into a
# commit, a screenshot, a Slack message or a support ticket, treat it as
# burned: delete it in AI Studio and issue a new one. Rotating takes 30
# seconds; an unbounded bill does not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# New keys from AI Studio are created as "Auth keys".
# Note: from September 2026 the Gemini API rejects requests made with the
# older "Standard" keys — if your key predates that change, migrate now.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing else is required. The SDK reads GEMINI_API_KEY automatically:
#     from google import genai
#     client = genai.Client()      # no arguments needed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
